%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against the verified P1b request flow
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as Customer
    participant SIM as Simulator (a web page)
    participant API as ReadyCall API
    participant SESS as SessionResolver
    participant SVC as IntentService
    participant BUS as Event bus
    participant ASM as ContextAssembler
    participant CORE as Bank core (READ-ONLY)

    U->>SIM: picks a persona
    SIM->>API: POST /v1/demo/session
    API-->>SIM: HttpOnly cookie
    Note right of API: DEMO shim for the bank's login (D47).<br/>The endpoints below cannot tell it apart<br/>from a real session.

    U->>SIM: opens the coverage page
    SIM->>API: POST /v1/app/context-events
    Note right of API: cheap and frequent - a ring-buffer<br/>append, no I/O. Windowed on read:<br/>browsing from 3 weeks ago is noise.

    U->>SIM: taps Contact
    SIM->>API: POST /v1/calls/intents {product_code, entry_screen, app_intent}
    Note over SIM,API: NO customer_id in the body. There is no<br/>such field to send. (D4)

    API->>SESS: resolve(cookie)
    SESS-->>API: Principal(customer_id)
    API->>SVC: create(customer_id=..., ...)
    SVC->>SVC: mint token, store ONLY its SHA-256 hash
    SVC->>BUS: publish intent.created
    SVC-->>API: intent + plaintext token
    API-->>SIM: 201 {intent_id, correlation_token, dial_target, expires_at}
    Note right of SIM: ~50ms. The customer can start<br/>dialling NOW.

    API->>BUS: drain (background task, after the response)
    BUS->>ASM: intent.created
    par six reads at once
        ASM->>CORE: customer / policies / interactions
        ASM->>CORE: holdings / life events / product
    end
    CORE-->>ASM: rows
    ASM->>ASM: pick relevant policy, stamp provenance
    ASM-->>BUS: frozen ContextSnapshot (measured: 1.8ms)

    U->>SIM: (still lifting the phone to their ear)
    SIM->>API: GET /v1/calls/intents/{id}
    API-->>SIM: context_ready, build_ms, policies, provenance fields
    Note over SIM,API: D18: the claim is inspectable, not asserted.
